.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt MOOBFS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm moobfs
.Nd query and inspect a mounted MoobFS layer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm info
.Op Fl -json
.Ar path
.Nm
.Cm query
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -ino
.Op Fl -order Ar name type Cm asc | desc
.Op Fl -limit Ar N
.Op Fl -page Ar N
.Ar directory
.Op Ar term ...
.Nm
.Cm check
.Op Ar moobfs-check-argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
answers attribute queries from the MoobFS layer's index and reports the state of a mount.
It uses the existing ioctls and tools; it adds no kernel interface.
MoobFS is an experimental research project.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm info
finds the moobfs_layer mount that holds
.Ar path
and prints what GET_INFO reports on its root: lower filesystem, interface versions, whether the
index is on, the domain depth, the index budget and build work, the attribute limits, and for an
administrator the index counters.
.It Cm query
asks QUERY2 on a domain
.Ar directory
and follows the cursor until the answer is complete, printing one path per line, relative to
.Ar directory .
On the root of a mount without domains it asks the mount-wide QUERY, which has no cursor.
Without
.Fl -order
the results are sorted by inode number.
.It Cm check
runs
.Xr moobfs-check 1
with the remaining arguments.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
reads the mount record from
.Pa /proc/self/mountinfo .
When a sandbox denies that read, it recognises the layer by
.Xr statfs 2 ,
.Cm query
still asks QUERY2, and
.Cm info
takes the highest directory above
.Ar path
on the same device as the mount root; the build work and idle options are then unknown.
See docs/tools.md.
.Pp
A
.Ar term
is four words,
.Dq name op type value ,
up to four terms joined by AND; op is one of
.Cm eq , lt , le , gt , ge , prefix
or
.Cm exists ,
whose type and value are given as
.Dq - .
An operator ending in
.Sq \&?
also matches files without the attribute.
Types are
.Cm string , int64 , double , bool
and
.Cm time .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -json
print one JSON object
.It Fl -ino
prefix each path with its inode number and a tab
.It Fl -order Ar name type Cm asc | desc
return the files whose
.Ar name
attribute has
.Ar type ,
ordered by its value and inode number; terms may then be empty
.It Fl -limit Ar N
stop after
.Ar N
results
.It Fl -page Ar N
results per call, 1 to 4096 (default 4096)
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 a system call failed; 3 the mount-wide query had more results than it can
return; 64 usage; 65 invalid terms or a query the kernel refused; 69 no layer there, a directory
that is not a domain, or the index off; 75 a temporary refusal (index budget, build limits, a
domain that kept changing); 77 permission denied.
The message on standard error names the cause.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl $ moobfs info /srv/memory
.Dl $ moobfs query /srv/memory/alice kind eq string decision
.Dl $ moobfs query --order created time desc --limit 10 /srv/memory/alice
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr moobfs-attr 1 ,
.Xr moobfs-check 1 ,
.Xr moobfs-index 1
.Pp
docs/tools.md and docs/operations.md in the MoobFS repository,
.Lk https://github.com/studiomoob/llmoobfs
